EXAMPLES=[{'num':'7','title':'Circle-Line Intersections','question':'Find intersections of 3x−4y+20 = 0 and x²+y² = 25.','steps':['Solve the line for y: y = (3/4)x+5.','Substitute into the circle: x²+((3/4)x+5)² = 25.','Expand and cancel 25: (25/16)x²+(15/2)x = 0.','Multiply by 16 and factor: 25x²+120x = 5x(5x+24) = 0.','The roots are x = 0 and x = −24/5; the corresponding y values are 5 and 7/5.','Check (0,5): the line gives −20+20 = 0 and the circle gives 25.','Check (−24/5,7/5): the line gives (−72−28)/5+20 = 0 and the squared radius is (576+49)/25 = 25.','The two different verified points are precisely the intersections. The center-to-line distance is 20/5 = 4 < 5, independently confirming two intersections.'],'answer':'(0,5) and (−24/5,7/5).','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':222,'pageEnd':223,'jpg':'115_page_2.jpg','verification':'Complete question and continuation visually checked'}]}]
